|info = *Nokko expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to throw an arcing bouncy spore that sprouts a rejuvenating mushroom on contact with a horizontal surface, inflicting <u>'''200'''</u> damage and {{D|Stagger}} to enemies within <u>'''6'''</u> meters of the sprouting location. The '''Brightbonnet''' is an intangible invulnerable object that lasts for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''10 / 15 / 20 / 25''' seconds, instantly releasing a pulse on creation, then periodically pulsing every <u>'''3'''</u> seconds over a range of {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''15''' meters to restore {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''10 / 12 / 13 / 15''' [[Energy]] points to Nokko and allies, while increasing their {{Stat|Ability Strength}} by {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''15% / 20% / 25% / 30%''' for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''5''' seconds. A maximum of <u>'''2'''</u> Brightbonnets can be placed.
**Number of active Brightbonnets are tracked on the ability icon.
**If a Brightbonnet Mushroom cannot be created where the spore lands, the energy cost is refunded.
**Brightbonnet spores will bounce off walls and other mushrooms.
**Brightbonnet appears on the minimap using its unique mushroom icon. This icon is not distinct from {{A|Stinkbrain}} mushrooms.
**The Ability Strength bonus is capped at <u>'''150%'''</u>, which is doubled to <u>'''300%'''</u> while Invigorated by the {{A|Sporespring}} or {{Weapon|Arbucep}} synergy interaction.
**The Ability Strength bonus will refresh on <u>all allies</u> if <u>any ally</u> is hit by subsequent pulses.
***Players will keep the single strongest Brightbonnet Strength buff that has been applied to them, and pulses from weaker Brightbonnets will refresh the Ability Strength bonus from stronger Brightbonnets.
**The Ability Strength bonus from Brightbonnets will <u>not</u> increase the Ability Strength bonus of Brightbonnets, but it will increase the amount of energy generated by any new Brightbonnets cast while affected by the bonus.
**Brightbonnet's energy restoration will affect Warframes (even with [[:Category:Channeled Abilities|channeled abilities]] active), [[Archwing]]s, and [[Railjack]]s, but <u>not</u> [[Necramech]]s.
**Nokko and allied players can jump on Brightbonnet Mushrooms to be propelled into the air, gaining bonus Double Jump velocity and immunity to Hard Landing until they next touch the ground.
***Each bounce also refreshes the player's ability to Double Jump or Bullet Jump, and allows the player to start a fresh aim glide.
***Jumping on a mushroom will force a pulse and place the mushroom on cooldown, which will cause subsequent players to pass through the mushroom instead of being propelled. The cooldown is visually indicated by the mushroom's brief glow and jiggle.
**Brightbonnet will despawn early if it is not rooted on a horizontal surface. Some [[Tilesets]] utilize shifting platforms and elevators, and mushrooms grown by Nokko do not move from their landing zone.
| interactions =
*Brightbonnets will become Invigorated when hit by {{A|Sporespring}} or {{Weapon|Arbucep}} projectiles.
**An Invigorated Brightbonnet has its pulse interval reduced to <u>'''1.5'''</u> seconds and provides <u>'''twice'''</u> the {{Stat|Ability Strength}} buff.
**A Brightbonnet will remain Invigorated until an allied Warframe bounces upon it, at which point it will return to normal and revert to its non-Invigorated pulse interval and Ability Strength bonus.
***As long as a player does not lose their Ability Strength bonus, pulses from the de-Invigorated Brightbonnet will continue to refresh the Invigorated Ability Strength bonus. 
**Each time a Brightbonnet transitions from normal to Invigorated, its duration is reset to the full value.
**The first time a Brightbonnet becomes Invigorated, it will permanently receive a glowing rim around its silhouette. This glow will remain even if the Brightbonnet loses its Invigoration.
**Each time a Brightbonnet is Invigorated, it will visibly emit glowing spores until ⅔ of its duration has passed.
**While Arbucep is Nokko's [[Signature Weapon]], this interaction is not unique to Nokko. Arbuceps held by any squadmate will Invigorate the Brightbonnets of any other squadmate.
*In addition to jumping, {{A|Sporespring}} and {{Weapon|Arbucep}} projectiles will also force a pulse on each impact.
*{{A|Reroot}}'s Sprodling form can bounce off of Brightbonnets under lower ceilings than full-sized Warframes.
*Upon entering [[Bleedout]] with an active Brightbonnet, Nokko [[Nokko/Abilities#Passive|passively]] triggers '''Vital Decay''' to revert to his Sprodling form for <u>'''15'''</u> seconds and can revive himself by touching a previously placed Brightbonnet.
**Brightbonnets have their durations paused during Vital Decay, and all Brightbonnets are removed upon a successful self-revival.
| helminth =
*Subsuming Nokko to the [[Helminth]] will offer a Brightbonnet and its augments to be used by other Warframes. 
** The {{Stat|Ability Strength}} bonus is diminished to '''10% / 13% / 17% / 20%''' and energy restore is reduced to {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''6.67 / 8 / 8.67 / 10'''.
** The Ability Strength bonus cap is diminished to <u>'''100%'''</u>, which is still doubled if Invigorated by {{Weapon|Arbucep}}. <!--I was not able to get Sporespring to target mushrooms spawned by other players, where that's two Nokkos, or a Nokko and an ally with the Subsume ability.-->
| augment = 
| tips = 
*Throw a Brightbonnet into a crowd of enemies to scatter them with the {{D|Stagger}} effect.
*Throw Brightbonnet in front of you and jump to bounce into the air, then Double Jump to gain height advantage for casting other abilities, aerial gunfire, or transition into a melee/heavy ground slam to increase its slam radius drastically.
*Jump on Brightbonnet to repeated bounce into the air, reducing enemy accuracy against Nokko.
*Create a Brightbonnet under a low ceiling, such as [[Tilesets]] corridors and hallways, then bounce on it to force multiple rapid pulses that quickly refill energy for you and your nearby squadmates.
**{{A|Reroot}} Sprodling form is ideal for this interaction, since its small size allows Nokko to fit into small spaces that normal Warframes cannot.
*Create two Brightbonnets side-by-side and bounce off of them in the middle, forcing both mushrooms to pulse.
*To maximize the {{Stat|Ability Strength}} bonus and energy production, newly created Brightbonnets should be hit by a {{A|Sporespring}} as soon as possible to permanently double the bonus and halve the pulse interval for that mushroom.
*Brightbonnets allow {{A|Sporespring}} to bounce to them to extend its enemy detection range. Position the mushrooms spread across a room for Sporesprings to trampoline off them for maximum destructive chaos!
**Sporesprings in turn trigger Brightbonnets to pulse on each bounce, freeing Nokko to do other things or join in the bouncy fun.
